## Why This Is Asked

This question probes practical DR design: cross-region replication, active-active components, idempotent processing, and observable validation under real outage scenarios.

## Key Concepts

- DR and RTO/RPO
- Pub/Sub exactly-once delivery
- Cloud Run warm-standby
- Spanner multi-region vs Cloud SQL replication
- Dataflow streaming to BigQuery
- Per-environment isolation
- Observability and chaos testing

## Code Example

```javascript
// Node.js Pub/Sub subscriber skeleton with idempotent dedup logic
const {PubSub} = require('@google-cloud/pubsub');
const dedupe = new Set();
exports.receiveEvent = async (msg, context) => {
  const id = msg.attributes?.messageId || msg.id;
  if (dedupe.has(id)) {
    msg.ack();
    return;
  }
  dedupe.add(id);
  // process
  msg.ack();
};
```

## Follow-up Questions

- How would you verify RTO/RPO in production and CI/CD?
- What metrics and alarms would you define to detect a failover failure?

## Why This Is Asked

Assesses ability to design a tenant-isolated, event-driven ingestion pipeline using Cloud Run, Pub/Sub, and Dataflow with idempotence and basic observability; focuses on practical steps and trade-offs for cost and latency.

## Key Concepts

- Per-tenant isolation via separate datasets and service accounts
- Idempotent writes using event_id and staging+MERGE
- Signature validation of incoming webhooks
- Observability: Cloud Logging, Monitoring, and dashboards
- Testing: end-to-end with signed test events and replay

## Code Example

```javascript
// Webhook signature verification (pseudo)
function verifySignature(signature, payload) {
  const crypto = require('crypto');
  const secret = process.env.WEBHOOK_SECRET;
  const h = crypto.createHmac('sha256', secret).update(JSON.stringify(payload)).digest('hex');
  return crypto.timingSafeEqual(Buffer.from(signature), Buffer.from(h));
}
```

